    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "MULTI BRANCH\n\nMulti Branch is an else-if chain in one node: it has three Condition inputs and four exec outputs\n(Branch1, Branch2, Branch3, Else). The FIRST condition that is true runs its output; if none is true,\nElse runs. Use it instead of a staircase of nested Branch nodes.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          210.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "THREE QUESTIONS\nscore >= 90, score >= 80, score >= 70. They are evaluated in order; the first true one wins. With a score of 72 only the third is true, so Branch3 runs and the grade is \"C\".",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          580.0
        ],
        "size": [
          640.0,
          110.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "sc1",
          "a_q",
          "sc2",
          "b_q",
          "sc3",
          "c_q"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "FOUR OUTCOMES\nBranch1..Branch3 and Else each set the grade. Change the score variable's default (try 95 or 40) and recompile to take another path. Only the Else path prints, to keep the graph simple.",
        "position": [
          960.0,
          -110.0
        ],
        "size": [
          560.0,
          130.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
